Z||000001||Fiero_24||10-30-2001||08:30 PM||||Explain "gimp mode".<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||10-30-2001||08:47 PM||||ROFL<P><BR>He means "Limphome" mode... totally messes with your mixtures, uses a set fuel table that bases on the TPS, and locks the timing, (no advance) or so I understand...<BR>In other words, Not good. Won't damage the car motor right away, but plays merry hell on your fuel economy, your cat, and your nerves when it's clear that the car has NO balls.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Cozmo||10-30-2001||09:13 PM||||"Gimp Mode"...<BR>I love it!<BR>I'm gonna use that phrase from now on...<BR>Yeah, like Mach10 described, everything reverts to fixed parameters. Best thing to do is read the stored codes in the ECM to see what went STOOPID on you.<P>BobC||||reg||10
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||10-30-2001||11:50 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cool85gt:<BR><B>my car is barily running right now. iv been told its in gimp mode. how bad is that for the car????????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've been in gimp mode for over 8 years now...<BR>My car still transports me around fine!<BR>The older I get, the more gimp I get...<BR>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">          <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
